<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:s="https://wvusports.com/services/xml_schema/story" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/"><channel><title /><link>https://wvusports.com/rss/</link><description /><atom:link href="https://wvusports.com/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml" /><language>en-us</language><ttl>60</ttl><item><title>Watters Wins at NWCA All-Star Classic</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/24/wrestling-watters-wins-at-nwca-all-star-classic</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/24/wrestling-watters-wins-at-nwca-all-star-classic</guid><category>Wrestling</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Ty Watters wrestles against Collin Gaj at the NWCA All-Star Classic on Nov. 24, 2026." src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/24/SZ9_6224-2.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – Redshirt junior No. 7 Ty Watters and redshirt sophomore No. 13 Max Vanadia represented the No. 25 West Virginia University wrestling team at the 2026 National Wrestling Coaches Association (NWCA) All-Star Classic at Rec Hall on the campus of Penn State University in University Park, Pennsylvania, on Tuesday night.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/SZ9_6224-2.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/SZ9_6224-2.jpg"><media:title>Ty Watters wrestles against Collin Gaj at the NWCA All-Star Classic on Nov. 24, 2026.</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/SZ9_6224-2.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 19:58:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>18</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59759</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Open Battle 4 Atlantis with Win Over Florida</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/24/womens-basketball-mountaineers-open-battle-4-atlantis-with-win-over-florida</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/24/womens-basketball-mountaineers-open-battle-4-atlantis-with-win-over-florida</guid><category>Women's Basketball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Khyala Ngodu blocks a shot during a game against Florida at the Battle 4 Atlantis" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/24/0U2A2304.JPG" /><br /><br />PARADISE ISLAND, Bahamas – The No. 22 West Virginia Mountaineers improved to 6-0 on the season with a 70-62 victory over Florida at Atlantis Resort in the Bahamas on Tuesday afternoon during the Battle 4 Atlantis. WVU used a strong second quarter and a balanced offensive effort to withstand a second-half push from the Gators to remain unbeaten.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/0U2A2304.JPG" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/0U2A2304.JPG"><media:title>Khyala Ngodu blocks a shot during a game against Florida at the Battle 4 Atlantis</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/0U2A2304.JPG" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 18:32:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>9</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59758</s:story_id></item><item><title>Mountaineers Welcome No. 20 Baylor for Final Regular-Season Ranked Matchup</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/24/volleyball-mountaineers-welcome-no-20-baylor-for-final-regular-season-ranked-matchup</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/24/volleyball-mountaineers-welcome-no-20-baylor-for-final-regular-season-ranked-matchup</guid><category>Volleyball</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="WVU Volleyball team huddles before the start of a match" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/24/VB_WVUvsUCF_Nov15_2026_JC_575.jpg" /><br /><br />MORGANTOWN, W.Va. – The West Virginia University volleyball team (13-13, 6-10 Big 12) welcomes its final ranked opponent of the regular season to Hope Coliseum on Wednesday, Nov. 25, as the Mountaineers host No. 20 Baylor. First serve is set for 2 p.m. ET.]]></description><media:thumbnail url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_system&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/VB_WVUvsUCF_Nov15_2026_JC_575.jpg" /><media:content url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/VB_WVUvsUCF_Nov15_2026_JC_575.jpg"><media:title>WVU Volleyball team huddles before the start of a match</media:title></media:content><enclosure url="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&amp;image_path=/images/2026/11/24/VB_WVUvsUCF_Nov15_2026_JC_575.jpg" length="1" type="image/jpg" /><pubDate>Tue, 24 Nov 2026 15:15:00 EST</pubDate><s:sport_id>17</s:sport_id><s:story_id>59757</s:story_id></item><item><title>Twelve Mountaineers Named to CSC Academic All-District Soccer Teams</title><link>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/24/womens-soccer-twelve-mountaineers-named-to-csc-academic-all-district-soccer-teams</link><guid>https://wvusports.com/news/2026/11/24/womens-soccer-twelve-mountaineers-named-to-csc-academic-all-district-soccer-teams</guid><category>Men's Soccer, Women's Soccer</category><description><![CDATA[<img alt="Soccer ball at Dick Dlesk Soccer Stadium" src="https://wvusports.com/common/controls/image_handler.aspx?thumb_prefix=rp_primary&image_path=/images/2026/11/24/MSOC_WVUvsWashington_Nov22_2026_TT-15.jpg" /><br /><br 